{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise verified before editing, and it held.\n\nLive read-only evidence (2026-08-19):\n- GET /repos/navapbc/rebar/environments/pypi -> required_reviewers rule with reviewer_count=1 (the user JoeOakhartNava, this project's configured release identity), prevent_self_review=false; environment can_admins_bypass=true.\n- GET /repos/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31916566035/approvals -> state 'approved' cast by JoeOakhartNava with comment 'release 0.12.0 - approved per release process (ticket grassgreen-unfearful-quoll)'.\n\nWhat the docs said: docs/releasing.md described the required-reviewers rule as 'the second human approval on every publish' and told the operator to 'approve the `pypi` deployment when prompted'. .github/workflows/release.yml:294 repeated the claim as 'the second human gate on every publish'.\n\nWhat the mechanism actually does: it holds the publish job, and the environment-scoped OIDC token with it, until an identity on the environment's reviewer list approves that specific run. That is identity + ref control over who can release the publish job. It is NOT a second pair of eyes and not an interactive checkpoint: one configured reviewer, self-review permitted, admin bypass available, and the approval is an ordinary REST call routinely made non-interactively. The 'published source was reviewed' property comes from releasing only from Gerrit-reviewed main, which the doc already stated correctly and which the rewrite now points at explicitly.\n\nScope note on AC4: the repo-wide grep is clean across docs/, CONTRIBUTING.md, AGENTS.md and .github/. The single remaining hit anywhere in the tree is the string 'explicit human approval token' inside docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/exp1_substance.jsonl - frozen captured LLM output from a plan-review experiment, unrelated to the release gate. Not edited: it is recorded experimental data, not release documentation.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md were swept and contain no occurrence, so neither needed an edit.\n\nGates (whole tree, worktree venv): make lint PASS (ruff check + format, complexity ratchet active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0, config-ownership, config-reads, DCO identity, criteria vocabulary, skill frontmatter, zizmor on release.yml clean, actionlint all workflows). make typecheck PASS (mypy, 581 source files, no issues). python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check run directly: new=0 increased=0 stale=0. scripts/check_docs_index.py exit 0. pytest tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py tests/unit/test_release_guards.py: 40 passed.\n\nGerrit change: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1949"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787205214282461001,"uuid":"6bdedd54-4cf5-4382-8f89-24abf8d0a000"}